                affiliations, and certifications, and, upon reasonable request, submit
                documentation verifying this information;
            m) Do not provide CMMC consulting services while serving as a CMMC instructor.
               This restriction prohibits the instructor from providing consulting services or
               offering targeted advice to students while in the act of providing classroom (in-
               person or virtual) instruction but does not necessarily prevent the instructor from
               providing consulting services as a separate professional activity outside the
               CMMC classroom;
            n) Do not solicit consulting business or market any product or service while delivering
               CMMC training for an ATP;
            o) Do not participate in the development of exam objectives and/or exam content or
               act as an exam proctor while at the same time serving as a CCI;
            p) Keep confidential all information obtained or created during the performance of
               CMMC training activities, including trainee records, except as required by law;
            q) Do not disclose any CMMC-related information or metrics to anyone without prior
               coordination with and approval from DoD;
            r) Notify the Accreditation Body or the CAICO if required by law or authorized by
               contractual commitments to release confidential information;
            s) Do not share with anyone any CMMC training-related information not previously
               publicly disclosed.




